; A guard (check (/= A B)) admits a match whose two sides no solution makes
; one term: on ground values, term disequality.  It reads no row; it filters
; the matches of its rule.  Positive: (pair 1 2) and (pair (f 1) (f 2)) pass.
; Negative: (pair 3 3) and (pair (f 1) (f 1)) do not.  With an unknown, the
; guard asks every solution: (pair ?a 4) can be made (pair 4 4), so it fails;
; (pair (g ?b) 5) can never be (pair 5 5), so it passes.
(store set)
(step every)
(pair 1 2)
(pair 3 3)
(pair (f 1) (f 2))
(pair (f 1) (f 1))
(pair $a 4)
(pair (g $b) 5)
(rule apart (read (pair $x $y)) (check (/= $x $y)) (make (apart $x $y)))
